WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.300
Around AD 53, Paul passes on
something he says he received.

2
00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:10.660
Jesus was buried, Paul writes,
raised on the third day, and seen.

3
00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:14.340
Decades later, three Gospels
tell that Easter morning,

4
00:00:14.390 --> 00:00:16.170
each in its own way.

5
00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:19.680
In Luke, two men in dazzling clothes ask:

6
00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:22.720
why do you seek the
living amongst the dead?

7
00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:24.970
So do the differences matter?

8
00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:27.720
And what did it mean
to the first believers?

9
00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:30.350
In this mission, you'll
follow Luke's chapter,

10
00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:33.000
from the tomb in Jerusalem to Bethany.

11
00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:38.600
Then you'll weigh up a hard question: do
the differences make the stories unreliable?

12
00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:41.870
Your mission: find out whether
the differences matter,

13
00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:44.360
and what Easter meant
to the first believers.
